{"title": "Youth Protests in Delhi Spark International Concern", "summary": "On February 21, a group of students from the National Students' Union of India (NSUI) protested against the government's decision to increase the minimum age limit for higher education. The protests were held near the Radcliffe Line, which marks the international border between India and Pakistan. Police claimed that over 100 protesters were detained during the event. The Wire reported that the protests were peaceful but were met with a heavy police response. The Telegraph India editorial argued that the police mishandled the protests, while Telangana Today's opinion piece highlighted the need for accountability in addressing the concerns of young people.", "summary_points": [], "title_hi": "", "summary_hi": "", "summary_points_hi": [], "framing": {}, "framing_hi": {}, "topic": "Society", "region": "India", "image_url": "", "sources": [{"source": "The Wire", "owner": "The Wire", "lean": "left", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "How Indias Youth Movement Looked from Beyond the Radcliffe Line"}, {"source": "The Telegraph (India)", "owner": "The Telegraph (India)", "lean": "left", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "Stick State: Editorial on police 'mishandling' of youth protests in Delhi and elsewhere"}, {"source": "Telangana Today", "owner": "Telangana Today", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxQMjVqc2pXYXpvWXpzRnhtYTJseHB0U19zRGVTOEZoQ2dhakF2eEwzRUhPOGdrZW1TLVp5eW1hRW5iNzVNWXdhb2dzTmh1cFQ1V0xKSUpwX296cUQ5MGlPdTU3TzBsOFBXc3Azc2h4OGQ4cGRoX2hIUFRWaElURlZYUmdIajFrc3NpMTRiR1FVMVRoMi1mUnhjU0xiVW9Tb2d2UEVUYkV5c2dCV1pVLW5nRA?oc=5", "headline": "Opinion: Beyond the Resignation—NEET, youth protests, and India’s missing accountability"}], "coverage": {"left": {"count": 2, "sources": ["The Telegraph (India)", "The Wire"], "owners": ["The Telegraph (India)", "The Wire"]}, "center"